c:T514,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://www.squidagent.app/compare/squid-vs-v0-for-design-led-teams#faq","url":"https://www.squidagent.app/compare/squid-vs-v0-for-design-led-teams","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Can Squid handle design-driven prompts reliably?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, when the brief explicitly defines component and state intent. The key is providing enough structure in the prompt and checking the resulting component boundaries."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which is easier for a design-team review loop?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"If your review loop is primarily in Vercel + Next ecosystems, v0 is natural. If your team wants explicit export checks and checkpoints first, Squid can be easier to audit."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do design-led teams benefit from checkpoints?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Checkpoints reduce the cost of stakeholder revisions by making rollback precise and auditable."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What should we check after either tool completes?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Install in a clean environment, run lint/type checks/build, verify interactions at all target widths, and inspect diff scope for follow-up edits."}}]}7:["$","script","2",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$c"}}]
